proof.text:
Compute on the compatible triangle of step 1. The normalized composition comparison of [lem-amb-unbounded-compact-support-comparisons] is the following three-arrow composite, restricted to bounded-below inputs:
$$R_{s,D}I_{i,D}R_{r,D}I_{j,D}
\xrightarrow{R_{s,D}\gamma_DI_{j,D}}R_{s,D}R_{p,D}I_{b,D}I_{j,D}
\xrightarrow{\mathrm{direct\ composition}}R_{sp,D}I_{b,D}I_{j,D}
\xrightarrow{\mathrm{open\ composition}}R_{sp,D}I_{a,D}.$$
It agrees on D^+ with the α of [lem-amb-etale-compact-comparisons]. Step 4 says that the coefficient comparison for each proper-composition or open-composition arrow commutes with that arrow. Step 6, whiskered by R_s and I_j, says the same for its first arrow. Naturality moves the coefficient comparisons for s and j across these whiskered arrows. Hence the rectangle of these three squares commutes. More explicitly, for a word W=H_t⋯H_1 in proper direct images and open extensions, define c_W by successively inserting χ_{H_i} or β_{H_i} from the outside inward. Naturality gives c_{UV}=U_B(c_V)c_UV_A. For composable arrows v:W→W' and w:W'→W'', the two equalities c_{W'}Q(v)=v_Bc_W and c_{W''}Q(w)=w_Bc_{W'} imply c_{W''}Q(wv)=(wv)_Bc_W by substitution. Applying this to the three displayed arrows gives
$$q_{gf,K}^{(a,sp)}Q_Z(\alpha_{g,f,m,K})
=\alpha_{g,f,n,Q_XK}\,F_{g,n}^{(i,s)}(q_{f,K}^{(j,r)})\,q_{g,F_{f,m}K}^{(i,s)}.$$
The formula for each c at an endpoint is exactly step 3, together with step 4's proper/open composition equations. All four intermediate functor words are the ones displayed here; no exceptional adjunction is involved.
